    "step5_reality_check": {
      "0": "Screenshots show an accessible Coursera browse/results interface with visible course cards while logged out (top-right shows \u201cLog In\u201d and \u201cJoin for Free\u201d). No captcha or sign-in wall is present in the captured views, and a results list/grid is clearly visible.",
      "1": "The UI displays active filter chips under \u201cAll results\u201d for \u201cLanguage: English,\u201d \u201cCourses,\u201d \u201cBeginner,\u201d and \u201c1-3 Months,\u201d which is strong on-screen verification for those three requested filters plus product type. However, \u201cData Science\u201d is not consistently shown as an active filter chip; in some screenshots it appears only as a category pill among many, and at least one filtered-results view shows seemingly non\u2013data-science course titles (e.g., chemistry), so subject=Data Science is not always pixel-verifiable from the filter area alone.",
      "2": "Ratings are shown on course cards in some screenshots (e.g., 4.8 (5.2K), 4.6 (4.3K), 4.8 (4K); or 4.8 (19K), 4.6 (44K), 4.8 (21K)), but the interface is not shown being sorted by rating/highest-rated. Therefore, screenshots can verify that selected courses have certain displayed ratings and satisfy visible filters, but generally cannot confirm they are the overall \u2018three highest-rated\u2019 among all matches (only that they are three visible results). Also note: in at least one screenshot, ratings are not visible on the cards at all, preventing verification of \u201chighest-rated.\u201d",
      "3": "Course cards typically show a numeric star rating followed by a parenthetical count (e.g., \u201c(5.2K)\u201d); the parenthetical is not labeled as enrollments and appears to be rating/review count formatting. Enrollment/learner counts are not displayed on the visible cards in these screenshots, so \u2018enrollment unavailable\u2019 is the appropriate reporting when adhering strictly to what is shown.",
      "4": "For the second course card in the \u2018AI Fundamentals / Introduction to Statistics / Maximize Productivity\u2026\u2019 view, the title and rating (4.6 with \u201c(4.3K)\u201d) are visible, but no enrollment count is displayed. In other screenshot views, the set/order of courses differs (e.g., an IBM course appears as the middle card), so which course is \u201c#2\u201d depends on the specific captured results row.",
      "5": "For the third course card in the \u2018AI Fundamentals / Introduction to Statistics / Maximize Productivity\u2026\u2019 view, the title and rating (4.8 with \u201c(4K)\u201d) are visible, but no enrollment count is displayed. As with the other courses, the parenthetical count appears tied to ratings/reviews, not enrollments, and should not be treated as an enrollment figure.",
      "6": "All provided screenshots show a logged-out browsing state (presence of \u201cLog In\u201d / \u201cJoin for Free\u201d). Course cards include \u201cFree trial\u201d or \u201cPreview\u201d buttons, but there is no visual evidence of clicking into a checkout/enrollment flow, starting a trial, or signing in. The screenshots alone cannot confirm the agent\u2019s stopping behavior, but they do not show any prohibited action being taken."
    },
